 the wizard king in the first  place and in this arc i'd also like to  point out that astor is showing some  great signs of maturity as well because  there's one instance where he's facing  off against  fauna and he suggests that they sit down  and talk things out rather than fight  which is kind of odd for his brand of  character odd but nice  and then there's another moment against  large ross where he refuses to remove  his sword because he is not  a merciful [ __ ] i like it boy be  growing and he'll grow even more but  first let's talk about the witch's  forest  our main setting for this arc is pretty  stunningly drawn and introduces by far  the most terrifying character in the  series to this point in the witch queen  she is just out of this world on a whole  new level none of the midnight sun guys  have even come  close to the feeling of sinister that  this  like she's crying blood which works very  well with her blood creation magic  terrifying stuff there as well but i  think her design is actually strongest  in the moments where the queen gets  angry and basically becomes a shaded  silhouetted demonic thing where all you  can really see are her piercing eyes and  you know what she's probably my favorite  antagonist thus far and also responsible  for unlocking  two count him two major power-ups during  this arc the first of which is astor's  i don't know does this form have a name  but he has this moment of confronting  his literal inner demon for the first  time which  looks so damn cool i know that it's a  cliche to have the plucky youngstown and  protagonist saddled with this  overwhelming powerful and potentially  evil entity but i'm pretty on board with  this especially if it results in the  kind of fantastic art that we have of  this half or  partially demonic aster i really love  this design because you can see the  darkness infesting asta's body through  the relentless roots on his chest  attempting just to seep further and  further and the wing is 